// ICF codes, Socialstyrelsen inventory to SNOMED CT mappings, codes s2
// Several sources map to the same target; each mapping is its own assertion.
context {
    collection "icf-snomed-ct" version="2026.1"
    source system="ICF" release="2026"
    target system="SNOMED_CT" release="20251130"
}
defaults {
    mappings {
        preference "primary"
        assessment-method "source-default-granularity"
    }
}
mapping "s2.1" source="s2" target="SNOMED_CT:81745001" relationship=partial_overlap effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source s2 SNOMED CT 117590005 81745001 = ICF Ch.2 chapter root: the eye, the ear, and related
        structures (a heterogeneous grouping of special-sense-organ anatomy). SNOMED CT has NO single
        concept denoting — the eye and ear are separate body-structure branches sharing only the loose /
        ancestors. Multi-target partial: SNOMED CT 81745001 (OMOP id 4305329) covers the eye axis;
        117590005 (OMOP id 4037611) covers the ear axis. Each target is one component of the multi-part
        source (partial); neither subsumes the whole. Low tier : the chapter root is a classification
        grouping, not a single anatomical concept, so each component target is a defensible-but-loose
        lead. (69536005) alternative was considered and rejected as too coarse.
        """
}
mapping "s2.2" source="s2" target="SNOMED_CT:117590005" relationship=partial_overlap effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
}
mapping "s210.1" source="s210" target="SNOMED_CT:87716009" relationship=equivalent effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source s210 SNOMED CT 87716009 = ICF body structure: structure of orbit (bony orbit / orbital
        region). Target (OMOP id 40641217). Same anatomical concept; SNOMED CT's is the canonical
        body-structure concept for the orbit. The (110528008) (362901003) as narrower substructures, but
        87716009 is the region-level equivalent matching the ICF s210 granularity. High tier : exact
        term match at the same granularity, not independently crosswalk-verified beyond the mirror.
        """
}
mapping "s220.1" source="s220" target="SNOMED_CT:81745001" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source s220 SNOMED CT 81745001 = ICF body-structure chapter s22 (globe of eyeball as a whole).
        Target (Athena 4305329) =, active standard; its synonyms are / and it is the canonical SNOMED CT
        concept for the globe of the eyeball. Exact 1:1 equivalence between the ICF and SNOMED CT's eyeball
        body structure; web-confirmed via SNOMED CT browser that 81745001 is the established active eyeball
        concept.
        """
}
mapping "s2200.1" source="s2200" target="SNOMED_CT:29445007" relationship=partial_overlap {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source s2200 SNOMED CT 18619003 29445007 68703001 = ICF s220 subdivision bundling THREE distinct
        eyeball coats: conjunctiva (bindhinna), sclera (senhinna) and choroid (åderhinna). No single
        SNOMED CT concept denotes this exact trio (the tunica concepts group differently: fibrosa =
        sclera+cornea; vasculosa = choroid+iris+ciliary body). Per the partial multi-component rule,
        emit one target per component: SNOMED CT 29445007 (Athena 4105319) =; SNOMED CT 18619003 (Athena
        4091162) =; SNOMED CT 68703001 (Athena 4287575) = — all active standard body structures. Each
        partial target covers one slice of the multi-part source; tier per the partial-multi-target
        guidance.
        """
}
